course: dictionary
lesson: 2903
title: Downhill: slopes, speed and more
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Downhill means going down a slope, towards the bottom of a hill. «Water flows downhill because gravity pulls it down.» Gravity is the pull that makes things fall, so the water moves down the slope, not up.
explain: Downhill can describe a path as well as a movement. «A downhill path» is a path that slopes down. «The bike rolled downhill» tells you the bike was going down. Look at the words around downhill: a path, a bike, or a slope tells you it means going down.
explain: Downhill can also mean getting worse. «After one mistake, the game went downhill.» The game did not roll down a real hill. The clues are one mistake and a game, so the word means things became worse.
explain: Downhill can be a noun too: a downhill is a fast race down a mountain, as in skiing. When you meet downhill, ask yourself: is this about a real slope, or about things getting worse?
fact: Downhill means going down a slope towards the bottom of a hill.
fact: «A downhill path» is a path that slopes down.
fact: «It's all downhill from here» means the hard part is over and it will be easy now.
fact: Going downhill on a bike or scooter makes you go faster, so brake gently and early.
fact: «A glacier is a large mass of ice that moves slowly downhill.»
exercise: «The bike rolled downhill and gathered speed.» What does downhill mean here? | Into a shop | *Down a slope towards the bottom of the hill | Up the side of a mountain | Round and round in a circle
exercise: «After one mistake, the game went downhill.» What does downhill mean here? | *Getting worse | Starting again from the beginning | Going down a slope | Getting faster and better
exercise: «Water flows downhill because gravity pulls it down.» What pulls the water downhill? | A snowball | *Gravity | Sunshine | A bicycle
test: Ravi says, «It's all downhill from here.» What does he mean? | He has to climb back up the hill | He is about to be sent down the hill | He wants to go skiing | *The hard part is over and it will be easy now
test: «A glacier is a large mass of ice that moves slowly downhill.» How does a glacier move? | It does not move at all | *Slowly, down a slope | Quickly and in a straight line up | Only when the weather is hot
exam: Which sentence uses downhill as a noun, meaning a race? | «The downhill path wound past the farm.» | *«The downhill was the fastest race of the winter.» | «The ball rolled downhill.» | «We walked downhill to the lake.»
